SUMMARY:The Family Picture Show
DTSTART:20260510T183000Z
DTEND:20260510T201000Z
DTSTAMP:20260510T183000Z
UID:1WJp18qfsk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nExplore the stories and fables th
 at connect young people all over the world with this showcase of family-fr
 iendly shorts appropriate for ages 6 and up.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/the-family-picture-show-x41551\n\nEstimated start: 11:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Best Summer
DTSTART:20260510T210000Z
DTEND:20260510T224000Z
DTSTAMP:20260510T210000Z
UID:8FrOCmSO8Y
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 84 mins (1h24m)\n\nA found footage documentary from 
 a concert tour in 1995 featuring live performances\, candid interviews\, a
 nd a behind-the-scenes view of what it's like to be on tour with Beastie B
 oys\, Sonic Youth\, Foo Fighters\, Beck\, Pavement\, Rancid\, The Amps\, a
 nd Bikini Kill. Director Tamra Davis scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.s
 iff.net/festival/the-best-summer\n\nEstimated start: 14:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Soul Patrol
DTSTART:20260511T000000Z
DTEND:20260511T015500Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T000000Z
UID:tc0Yw38RQM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nThe Vietnam War's first all-Black
  special operations team spent decades in silence. Now\, fifty years later
 \, they gather one last time to tell the story America forgot to tell.Dire
 ctor J.M. Harper scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sou
 l-patrol\n\nEstimated start: 17:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salvation
DTSTART:20260511T023000Z
DTEND:20260511T044500Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T023000Z
UID:lI2OY8QeFm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nIn a historical moment when an 
 “us versus them” mentality is fueling polarization around the world\, 
 director Emin Alper grapples with this issue in a timeless tale with real-
 world resonance.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/salvation\n\nEstimated s
 tart: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Restoration at Grayson Manor
DTSTART:20260511T220000Z
DTEND:20260511T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260511T220000Z
UID:4Avn4JTwW2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nWhen a spoiled Irish playboy lose
 s his hands\, his controlling mother replaces them with mechanical ones 
 — operated entirely by his murderous subconscious.\n\nhttps://www.siff.n
 et/festival/the-restoration-at-grayson-manor\n\nEstimated start: 15:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Doctor
DTSTART:20260512T003000Z
DTEND:20260512T022000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T003000Z
UID:F2W6ypVbrW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nThree courageous doctors—a Jewi
 sh orthopedic surgeon from North Carolina\, a Zoroastrian trauma surgeon f
 rom California\, and a Palestinian American ER specialist from Illinois—
 volunteer their services in Gaza\, risking their lives to save others.Dire
 ctor Poh Si Teng scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/ame
 rican-doctor\n\nEstimated start: 17:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Iván & Hadoum
DTSTART:20260512T030000Z
DTEND:20260512T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T030000Z
UID:QU8VMch3dN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nAmid the sprawling greenhouses o
 f Almería\, trans man Iván and migrant Hadoum share an unexpected\, elec
 tric connection. But when Iván rises to become her boss\, passion collide
 s with power and prejudice\, revealing the fragile boundaries between love
 \, identity\, and class.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/ivan-and-hadoum\
 n\nEstimated start: 20:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
